WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.010
As I hinted at in the last lesson, your boss really likes cats.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.720
They want even more cats.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.690
In fact, they want Cat Clicker Premium.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.560
Now obviously, you'll run out of screen space if you add too many more,

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.200
so your boss wants you to build a list of cats on the side.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.812
And when you choose a cat from that list, the cat is displayed in the cat area.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:23.350
That will mean quite a few changes to your application.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.860
You'll need to find a way to build a list of cats.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.020
You'll need to add selection functionality to the list.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.910
You'll need to display the correct cat when the list items are clicked, and

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.920
of course, you'll need to keep each cat's number separate and accurate.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.760
I'll provide you with an official spec sheet for

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.600
the new application in a second.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.830
And my advice to you is the same.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:45.730
Try not to repeat yourself, and make sure that you choose some cute pictures of

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.690
cats so they can comfort and console you if you feel frustrated.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.290
After this step, we'll go over the code together and

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:55.640
we'll start talking about some useful organizational techniques for

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.150
resolving some of the problems you're likely running into.

